Verse 1:
[C]Watchmen, on the walls of [F]Zi[C]on, What O [Dm]tell us, [C]of [G]the [C]night?
[C]Is the daystar now a[F]ris[C]ing? Will the [Dm]morn soon [C]greet [G]our [C]sight?
[C]O'er your vision Shine there [Dm]now some [C]rays [G]of [C]light?
[C]O'er your vision Shine there [Dm]now some [C]rays [G]of [C]light?

Verse 2:
[C]Tell, [F]O [C]tell [Dm]us, [C]are [G]the [C]landmarks
[C][F]On [C]our [Dm]voyage [C]all [G]passed [C]by?
[C]Are [Dm]we [C]nearing [G]now [C]the haven?
[C]Can [Dm]we [C]e'en [G]the [C]land descry?
[C]Do [F]we [C]truly [Dm]See [C]the [G]heavenly [C]kingdom nigh?
[C]Do [F]we [C]truly [Dm]See [C]the [G]heavenly [C]kingdom nigh?

Verse 3:
[C][F]Light [C]is [Dm]beaming, [C]day [G]is [C]coming!
[C][F]Let [C]us [Dm]sound [C]aloud [G]the [C]cry;
[C]We [Dm]behold [C]the [G]daystar [C]rising
[C]Pure [Dm]and [C]bright [G]in [C]yonder sky!
[C]Saints, [F]be [C]joyful; [Dm]Your [C]redemption [G]draweth [C]nigh;
[C]Saints, [F]be [C]joyful; [Dm]Your [C]redemption [G]draweth [C]nigh.

Verse 4:
[C]We [F]have [C]found [Dm]the [C]chart [G]and [C]compass,
[C]And [F]are [C]sure [Dm]the [C]land [G]is [C]near;
[C]Onward, [Dm]onward [C]we [G]are [C]hasting,
[C]Soon [Dm]the [C]haven [G]will [C]appear;
[C]Let [F]your [C]voices [Dm]Sound [C]aloud [G]your [C]holy cheer;
